prompt:
Use Three.js to implement an RPG encounter scene. A dragon guards a treasure chest, and the player must defeat the dragon through turn-based combat to obtain the treasure.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import through ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/Fox.glb as the dragon model;
(2) Place the dragon slightly behind the center of the scene at (0, 0, -3), and scale it appropriately so that it occupies the main area of the frame;
(3) If the model contains animations, extract the idle and attack animation clips (by iterating through gltf.animations);
(4) After loading is complete, set window.__3D_STATE__.modelLoaded = true;

[Scene Setup]
(5) Create a cave-style scene: use a dark brown rocky texture for the ground (0x4a3728) and a dark background (0x1a0a00);
(6) Place a treasure chest behind the dragon (BoxGeometry, gold 0xffd700, with a simple lid shape), with a glowing particle effect inside the chest;
(7) Scatter some gold coins throughout the scene (small cylinders, gold, at random positions);
(8) Use warm-toned lighting (orange PointLight simulating torches) plus a dim AmbientLight to create a cave atmosphere;
(9) Position the camera at a slightly elevated frontal angle looking downward (OrbitControls, with a restricted rotation range);

[Combat System]
(10) Player HP: 100, displayed as a green health bar (id="playerHP");
(11) Dragon HP: 200, displayed as a red health bar (id="dragonHP");
(12) "Attack" button (id="attackBtn"): when clicked, deals 10-20 points of random damage to the dragon;
  a) The camera shakes slightly during the attack (shake effect);
  b) Display a damage number on the dragon (floating-text animation that moves upward and fades out);
  c) Make the dragon flash red once (material.emissive temporarily turns red);
(13) Dragon counterattack: 1 second after the player attacks, the dragon automatically counterattacks for 15-25 points of random damage;
  a) The dragon plays its attack animation (if available) or performs a forward-leaning body animation;
  b) Display a damage number on the player's side;
  c) Briefly display a red vignette effect around the edges of the screen;
(14) "Heal" button (id="healBtn"): restores 20 HP and can be used at most 3 times;
  a) Display a green particle effect when used;
  b) HP must not exceed 100;
  c) After all uses are consumed, the button turns gray and is disabled;
(15) While idle, the dragon plays the idle animation (subtle floating/breathing), and briefly switches to the attack animation when attacked;

[Victory and Defeat Conditions]
(16) When the dragon's HP reaches 0: display "Victory! The treasure is yours!", play an animation that opens the treasure chest (rotate the lid), and display a bursting gold-coin particle effect;
(17) When the player's HP reaches 0: display "You were defeated by the dragon...", and darken the scene;
(18) For both endings, display a "Restart" button (id="restartBtn");

[Battle Log]
(19) Add a battle log panel on the right (id="battleLog") that scrolls and displays a text record of every attack/heal action, with the newest entry at the top;

[HUD Display]
(20) Display:
  - Player HP value and health bar (id="playerHP")
  - Dragon HP value and health bar (id="dragonHP")
  - Remaining heal uses (id="healUses")
  - Battle log (id="battleLog")
  - Battle state (id="battleState", fighting / victory / defeat)

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
{
  modelLoaded: boolean,
  playerHP: number,
  dragonHP: number,
  healUsesLeft: number,
  battleState: string,
  lastDamageToPlayer: number,
  lastDamageToDragon: number,
  totalDamageDealt: number,
  totalDamageTaken: number,
  turnsPlayed: number
}

Output a single HTML file, place it in the same directory as the assets/ folder, and run it through a local HTTP server.
